arbor (51.0.0~beta.3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Third public beta: full-tree scans keep far less memory - the whole-scan
    set of full path strings is gone, entry path buffers are moved rather
    than cloned, and returning to the start page releases the scan snapshot.
    Merging 500k entries is ~3x faster with ~21% lower peak RSS.

 -- hakergeniusz <hakergeniusz@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 22 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

arbor (51.0.0~beta.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Second public beta: cache hits no longer trigger a rescan (the Rescan
    button/Ctrl+R do a true from-disk rescan), and the scan-ingest tail is
    ~3x faster — cold open settles at 1.75 s on a 101k-item fixture
    (Baobab 50.0: 2.25 s on the same benchmark).

 -- hakergeniusz <hakergeniusz@users.noreply.github.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 21:45:00 +0100

